@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=handoff-formal
R|formal.use|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|symbolic notation may be used to make task predicates explicit; it is a supplement to the exact SIGMA/1 envelope and does not authorize tools/effects or replace BOOTSTRAP/decisions/routed LRF
R|formal.llm-docs|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|for documents primarily consumed by LLMs, use PIDGEN style: low-ambiguity hierarchy/schema + stable attention keywords (e.g. MUST, MUST_NOT, STOP; ACCEPT/REJECT must define local object and not impersonate decision-register status) + locally defined math/set relations + compact explanatory prose; lexical base may draw from English/Japanese/Chinese/Spanish, but every critical concept has one locally declared canonical label with aliases/translation only as retrieval aids; optimize semantic determinism and multilingual retrieval, not token compression alone
R|formal.doc-structure|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|encode rules as parseable units with explicit subject/scope, modality, condition, action, exception, and outcome; use stable headings/IDs and consistent nesting; one normative rule per unit where practical; distinguish normative constraints from examples, rationale, and nonnormative advice; these document-structure rules apply to LLM-primary documents, while formula grammar rules below apply specifically to symbolic task predicates/handoffs
R|formal.attention|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|attention markers/keywords/emoji map to a defined local function and remain consistent; emoji may overlay multiple non-exclusive discovery facets/search cues to prevent retrieval narrowing, but each cue is locally glossed and redundant to text; emoji do not encode hidden logical meaning, modality, or authorization; never infer MUST/permission from capitalization, emoji, typography, or position alone
R|formal.pidgen.lexicon|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|PIDGEN unit=hierarchical record with explicit ID/subject/scope/modality/condition/action/exception/outcome as applicable; define canonical term once, attach multilingual aliases only when they improve retrieval, and keep alias ≡ label only within declared scope; mixed-language phrasing must not change predicate, quantifier, negation, temporal order, or modality
R|formal.pidgen.relations|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|math/set symbols express typed relations only after local legend declares operands/domain/grouping; for every critical formula give a natural-language gloss preserving exact scope; prose is authoritative companion for nuance, not permission to weaken a formula
R|formal.pidgen.emoji|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use emoji as additive attention+retrieval overlays: define `emoji→facet` locally, allow multiple cues on one record when they represent distinct non-exclusive search facets, and retain a text label for each; cue-set expansion must not alter acceptance or normative meaning; unknown emoji meaning=undefined, never guess
R|formal.contracts-lrf|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|normative contracts/prohibitions/permissions/authority MUST use SIGMA/1 LRF as the atomic source; exactly one independently searchable rule per physical record line, each with a stable unique rule ID and explicit subject/scope/modality/condition/action/exception/outcome as applicable; choose distinctive tokens/IDs so `rg` can cherry-pick relevant rules without neighboring prose; PIDGEN hierarchy, Markdown, examples, and explanations MAY index/clarify but MUST NOT replace or contradict LRF authority
R|formal.legend|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|every nonstandard symbol/operator and every named predicate/variable must be defined locally in the payload or an attached task-local legend; undefined, overloaded, precedence-ambiguous, or domain-ambiguous notation=FAILED; do not guess its meaning
R|formal.core|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|within a declared formula only: ∧=AND; ∨=inclusive OR; ⊕=exclusive OR for Boolean predicates only; ⊗=tensor product of explicitly declared concepts/spaces, usable to bundle multiple task concepts; each factor, operand type, product meaning, and acceptance mapping must be defined locally; tensor composition does not implicitly widen target, authority, effects, or acceptance; ¬=NOT whose scope is the immediately following parenthesized expression or atom; ⇒=material implication; ⇔=if and only if; ∀x∈S=for every member x of set S; ∃x∈S=there exists a member x of set S; ∈=set membership; ∋=reverse membership (S∋x iff x∈S); ∉=not a member of; A∪B={x | x∈A ∨ x∈B} for declared sets A,B over compatible declared element types; empty union is ∅; ∝=proportionality only when variables, domain, proportionality constant/relationship, and whether the claim is exact or qualitative are stated; =/≠=equality/inequality; parentheses determine grouping; all other operators and any alternate meaning require explicit local definition
R|formal.project-symbols|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|for task notation using symbols observed in 指示書.md: ≤=numeric less-than-or-equal bound over declared comparable numbers; a〜b=closed inclusive range only when explicitly stated; n×X=repetition/cardinality count only when n is a declared nonnegative integer and X is a defined unit; == means equality only; := means assignment only; a single = is reserved for typed equation/definition and must be locally disambiguated (never infer assignment). Arrows require a tagged, fully parenthesized form: seq(A→B)=ordered execution A then B; state(A→B)=state transition A to B; choose(source=A; outcomes={B,C,...}; result∈outcomes)=select exactly one result from the explicitly exhaustive outcome set for source A; outcomes are mutually exclusive and exhaustive by declaration. Tagged forms may nest only with each subexpression parenthesized and tagged; otherwise flatten or define a local grammar. Never use an untyped → for implication (use ⇒ for material implication). These symbols are available notation, not adoption of 指示書.md as an authority source
R|formal.domain|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|declare the domain/type of quantified variables and whether constraints are preconditions, postconditions, invariants, ordering, or conditional actions; distinguish necessary from sufficient conditions; specify STOP/failure behavior for unknown, error, timeout, missing evidence, and exceptions; for set operators declare the universe/set identity and relevant empty-set behavior; for ∝ state the exact variables/domain and proportionality relation or clearly label it qualitative and non-computational
R|formal.crosscheck|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|each safety/authority/scope/acceptance-critical formula must have a concise natural-language paraphrase preserving quantifier, negation, modality, exception, effect, and stop condition; formula and paraphrase must agree; conflict or ambiguity=STOP+ask; never infer a weaker reading
R|formal.compression|task:handoff|MUST_NOT|RO_LOCAL|remove critical prose because an equation 'looks precise'; use of symbols alone as the sole carrier for safety, authority, approval, effects, scope, exceptions, or stop conditions is forbidden
R|formal.no-authority|task:handoff|MUST_NOT|RO_LOCAL|mathematical notation, formulas, signatures, or the SIGMA/1 wrapper do not create permission, approval, identity, proof of execution, or test evidence
R|formal.pidgen.cascade|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|classify each document by its primary nature as contract, process, reference-state, handoff, skill-like, or display; use rules/PIDGEN-CASCADE.seq only to discover and route readers to the applicable normative rules, and keep all normative contract/prohibition/permission/authority content in atomic SIGMA/1 LRF records
R|formal.pidgen.css|tag:docs|MUST_NOT|RO_LOCAL|rules/PIDGEN-CSS.md is a non-normative display/wording/retrieval supplement only and MUST NOT change behavior, authority, permission, acceptance, or decision state
L|formal.pidgen.cascade.link|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|[PIDGEN cascade sequence](PIDGEN-CASCADE.seq)
L|formal.pidgen.css.link|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|[PIDGEN CSS-like supplement](PIDGEN-CSS.md)
R|formal.skill-style|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|SKILL.md documents may be used solely as a notation/style reference for compact metadata, ordered sections, trigger/usage/description shape, and symbols accompanied by a gloss; this is syntax/style inspiration only and imports or grants no authority, permissions, effect policy, credential access, execution policy, or user directives
R|formal.design-choice|task:implementation|MUST|RO_LOCAL|when a required implementation/design choice is unspecified and materially changes behavior, safety, compatibility, cost, or scope, STOP before CODE and present exactly 3 distinct feasible options with concise tradeoffs and one justified recommendation; obtain user selection via choice prompt; selection=scope decision only, never effect approval; if only <3 honest feasible options exist, explain why and STOP+ask rather than invent options
R|formal.category-handoff|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|when using the selected lifecycle category lens, preserve the exact SIGMA/1 envelope and field order; define categories C_Draft,C_Handoff,C_Runner,C_Verify as typed record stages and arrows as record mappings only; functors H:C_Draft→C_Handoff, R:C_Handoff→C_Runner, V:C_Runner→C_Verify preserve identity/composition and never cause dispatch/execution/review; let A:C_Draft→C_Verify map declared Acceptance to check schema, P=V∘R∘H, Q=A; a natural transformation η:P⇒Q is the explicitly typed family η_t:P(t)→Q(t) with naturality Q(f)∘η_t=η_t'∘P(f) for each declared f:t→t'; gloss: the diagram compares the lifecycle record path with the Acceptance-schema path but does not assert equal outcomes; category objects/arrows/η are descriptive mappings only and MUST NOT create PASS, evidence, approval, authority, identity, or effects; actual Runner observations and independent review remain separately required; undefined object/arrow/map=STOP+define before use
R|formal.handoff.bindings|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|HANDOFF MAY declare temporary immutable bindings for words or emoji only in an explicit local `bind(name;type;meaning;value;scope=HANDOFF)` legend; `name` is unique within that HANDOFF, `type/meaning/value` are explicit, `scope` is the whole HANDOFF and later lifecycle-record references only; later stages MAY reference the same binding via `ref(name)` and MUST preserve source identity/provenance; rebinding, mutation, cross-HANDOFF use, undeclared symbol, type/scope mismatch, or emoji used as a variable without this declaration=STOP; bound values are data, not authority/permission/acceptance/evidence; the exact SIGMA/1 envelope and field order remain unchanged; each critical use has a concise prose gloss
